---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
const lang = 'en';
const UPDATED = '2026-10-05';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy policy of the notary fees calculator in France" description="Privacy for the notary fees calculator in France: data processed, Clarity and Google Analytics audience measurement, legal basis, retention and GDPR rights." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This page describes the processing of personal data linked to the use of {SITE_URL}, in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and French Law no. 78-17 of 6 January 1978.</p>
    <h2>Data controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>What the calculator does not do</h2>
    <p>The calculation runs in your browser. Price, département, situation and options are not sent to any server and are not stored anywhere; the analytics tools below do not receive them, as the fields are masked. The share link encodes your inputs in the page address: only send it to people of your choice; whoever opens it loads a page whose address contains those values.</p>
    <h2>Processing carried out</h2>
    <p><strong>Connection logs.</strong> The host records the IP address, date, page requested and browser, for the security and diagnosis of the service (legitimate interest, art. 6-1 f GDPR), under its own retention policy.</p>
    <p><strong>Audience measurement: Microsoft Clarity.</strong> Clarity loads when the page opens, with no consent banner. It records clicks, scrolling, pages viewed, device and browser type and approximate location, and produces session recordings and heatmaps that tell us which simulations are run and where the form gets in the way. Amounts entered in the calculator are masked in your browser. Cookies <code>_clck</code> (one year) and <code>_clsk</code> (one day); Microsoft may set <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> on its own domains. Legal basis: the publisher’s legitimate interest in improving the site (art. 6-1 f GDPR).</p>
    <p><strong>Audience measurement: Google Analytics 4.</strong> Provided by Google Ireland Limited and loaded the same way, with no banner, Google Analytics measures page views, where visits come from, how long they last, the device used and approximate location; the IP address is not stored. Cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code>, two years. Retention: 14 months. Legal basis: legitimate interest (art. 6-1 f GDPR).</p>
    <p><strong>Objecting.</strong> Block third-party cookies or the clarity.ms and google-analytics.com domains in your browser, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>; the calculator still works. List of cookies: <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>
    <p><strong>Advertising.</strong> The site displays no advertising.</p>
    <p><strong>Messages.</strong> If you write to the contact address, your address and message are processed to reply to you and kept for at most three years after the last exchange.</p>
    <h2>Recipients and transfers</h2>
    <p>No data is sold or transferred. Acting as processors: the host GitHub, Microsoft (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited and Microsoft Corporation) for Clarity, and Google (Google Ireland Limited and Google LLC) for Google Analytics. GitHub, Microsoft Corporation and Google LLC are based in the United States; transfers to them rely on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, to which they are certified, and on the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses. See the <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft privacy statement</a> and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection, portability: write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, reply within one month. You may complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}: <a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>. Last updated: {displayDate(UPDATED, 'en-GB')}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
